Wireless access to CUI within the {{tenant_variant}} tenant is protected through transport-layer encryption (TLS 1.2+) enforced at the cloud service boundary. The session-controlled BYOD architecture described in Section {{sectionNumber}} ensures that all wireless sessions traverse encrypted channels before reaching CUI-bearing workloads. No CUI is transmitted over unencrypted wireless links. Conditional Access policies require compliant session parameters regardless of the wireless network used by the endpoint device. Enforcement was verified active as of {{verification_date}}.